<title>USA: Quintiles completes Innovex acquisition.</title>
<headline>Quintiles completes Innovex acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>RESEARCH TRIANGLE PARK, N.C. 1996-11-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quintiles Transnational Corp said Friday it had completed the acquisition of Innovex Ltd, a private British pharmaceutical company, in exchange for about 10 million shares of Quintiles stock and the retirement of about $60 million of Innovex obligations.</p>
<p>Under the deal, Quintiles exchanged about 9.2 million shares of its stock and issued options to purchase about 800,000 additional shares.</p>
<p>Quintiles reiterated its projection that the transaction is expected to increase its 1997 earnings by $0.05 to $0.07 per share. It also reiterated that it expects to take a one-time charge related to the transaction but that the amount has not yet been determined.</p>
</text>
